        "category": "ancestry",
        "description": {
            "value": "<p>The greatest centaurs need not wait until their stories are over to touch the stars in the sky. You draw an arrow (or other ammunition), whisper a short invocation over it, and then Strike with a ranged weapon. The arrow becomes a bolt of starlight, changing its damage to your choice of force or spirit and granting it the effects of the <em>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.Ghost Touch]</em> rune. When the arrow Strikes its target, it unravels into a constellation of starlight that wraps around the target's limbs, imposing a –10-foot circumstance penalty to its Speeds for [[/r 2d4 #Starshot Arrow Duration]]{2d4 rounds} or @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Immobilized]{Immobilizing} it if the Strike was a critical hit. The target can untangle itself by spending an Interact action to break free.</p>\n<p>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.feat-effects.Item.Effect: Starshot Arrow]</p>"
        },
